President of the Association

04:47:55.318 --> 04:47:58.222
of Alumni and Alumnae of MIT.

04:48:06.934 --> 04:48:10.470
LASH: Please join me and
the distinguished members

04:48:10.470 --> 04:48:14.610
of the 50th reunion
Class of 1953

04:48:14.610 --> 04:48:18.240
as we congratulate the
graduates and welcome them

04:48:18.240 --> 04:48:22.040
into that most select
company of men and women

04:48:22.040 --> 04:48:27.020
who are the MIT
alumnae and alumni.

04:48:27.020 --> 04:48:30.980
[APPLAUSE]

04:48:37.415 --> 04:48:42.760
D'ARBELOFF: The 137th
commencement exercises

04:48:42.760 --> 04:48:45.800
of the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology

04:48:45.800 --> 04:48:48.728
are now concluded.

04:48:48.728 --> 04:48:51.656
[CHEERING]

04:48:54.650 --> 04:48:57.690
A reception will now
follow in the West Campus

04:48:57.690 --> 04:49:02.820
Plaza and the Johnson
Athletic Center.

04:49:02.820 --> 04:49:05.400
The audience and
graduates are requested

04:49:05.400 --> 04:49:10.380
to remain seated until the
stage assembly has recessed.

04:49:10.380 --> 04:49:13.710
And now please join
the MIT Chorallaries

04:49:13.710 --> 04:49:16.290
in singing the school song.

04:49:16.290 --> 04:49:19.740
It's on page five in the
front section of your program.

04:49:19.740 --> 04:49:23.191
Please rise.

04:49:23.191 --> 04:49:27.135
[MUSIC - "ARISE YE SONS OF MIT"]

04:49:32.065 --> 04:49:39.321
CHORALLARIES: (SINGING)
Arise all ye of MIT,

04:49:39.321 --> 04:49:44.534
in loyal fellowship.

04:49:44.534 --> 04:49:56.658
The future beckons unto ye,
and life is full and rich.

04:49:56.658 --> 04:50:02.026
Arise and raise
your glass on high.

04:50:02.026 --> 04:50:09.855
Tonight shall ever
be a memory that

04:50:09.855 --> 04:50:15.710
will never die for ye of MIT.

04:50:18.750 --> 04:50:30.400
Thy sons and daughters, MIT,
return from far and wide

04:50:30.400 --> 04:50:42.620
and gather here once more to
be renourished by thy side.

04:50:42.620 --> 04:50:54.322
And as we raise our glasses high
to pledge our love for thee,

04:50:54.322 --> 04:51:03.190
we join all those of days
gone by in praise of MIT.

04:51:06.252 --> 04:51:07.585
[MUSIC - "TAKE ME BACK TO TECH"]

04:51:07.585 --> 04:51:11.760
Oh, I wish that
I were back again

04:51:11.760 --> 04:51:15.710
at Tech on Boylston Street,
dressed in my dinky uniform, so

04:51:15.710 --> 04:51:17.460
dapper and so neat.

04:51:17.460 --> 04:51:21.070
I'm crazy after calculus,
I never had enough.

04:51:21.070 --> 04:51:23.010
'Twas hard to be
dragged away so young.

04:51:23.010 --> 04:51:25.390
It was horribly, awfully tough.

04:51:25.390 --> 04:51:28.831
Hurrah for Technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh!

04:51:28.831 --> 04:51:32.230
Glorious old Technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh!

04:51:32.230 --> 04:51:34.702
All Back in the days
that were free from care

04:51:34.702 --> 04:51:38.108
in the 'ology varsity shop, with
nothing to do but analyze air

04:51:38.108 --> 04:51:39.690
in an anemometrical top.

04:51:39.690 --> 04:51:43.650
The differentiation of
the trigonometric powers,

04:51:43.650 --> 04:51:45.505
the constant pi
that made me sigh

04:51:45.505 --> 04:51:47.400
in those happy days of ours.

04:51:47.400 --> 04:51:51.144
Hurrah for Technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh!

04:51:51.144 --> 04:51:54.870
Glorious old Technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh!

04:51:54.870 --> 04:51:58.400
Take me back on a special train
to that glorious institute.

04:51:58.400 --> 04:52:01.500
I yearn for the inspiration
of a technological toot.

04:52:01.500 --> 04:52:04.750
I'd shun the quizzical
physical profs, the chapel,

04:52:04.750 --> 04:52:05.500
and all that.

04:52:05.500 --> 04:52:08.975
But how I'd love to go
again on a scientific bat.

04:52:08.975 --> 04:52:11.450
La, la, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la, la--

04:52:16.400 --> 04:52:20.855
doot-doo-doo-doo, doot-doo,
duh-dah, duh-dah, duh-dah.

04:52:20.855 --> 04:52:29.000
O, M-A-S-S-A-C-H-U-S-E-T-T-S,
I-N-S-T-I-T-U-T-E O-F-T-E,

04:52:29.000 --> 04:52:36.675
and then there's C-H-N-O-L-O-G
and Y comes after G.

04:52:36.675 --> 04:52:41.665
It's the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology.

04:52:41.665 --> 04:52:43.661
Hey!

04:52:43.661 --> 04:52:47.154
[CHEERING]

04:52:50.148 --> 04:52:54.140
[PROCESSIONAL MUSIC]

04:55:18.850 --> 04:55:23.341
[PROCESSIONAL MUSIC]

04:58:16.200 --> 04:58:21.050
[PROCESSIONAL MUSIC]

